## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to translate regulatory requirements into automated, auditable technical controls using Azure AI and governance services, with strict multi-tenant isolation requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Regulatory-to-controls mapping (GDPR/CCPA/NIST)
- Knowledge base grounding with Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- Automated evidence collection and auditable logging
- Azure Policy integration for continuous enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Map obligations to controls and enforce per-tenant policy
async function ensureCompliance(clientId) {
  const obligations = await kb.fetchObligations(clientId);
  const controls = await mapToControls(obligations);

  const evidence = await collectEvidence(clientId, controls);
  const violations = await evaluateAgainstPolicy(controls, evidence);

  await logDecision({ clientId, obligations, controls, evidence, violations });
  return generateRemediationPlan(violations);
}
```

